      "title": "Calumet College - Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Calumet College - Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics Calumet College Apply Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics Whiting, IN Apply Description Position Summary Calumet College of St. Joseph (CCSJ) invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Mathematics beginning Spring 2026. Candidates must hold a master’s degree in mathematics or a closely related field and demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching within a liberal arts context. Preference will be given to applicants with experience teaching diverse undergraduate populations. The instructor may teach up to three courses per semester, including developmental, general education, and advanced mathematics, based on departmental needs. Most courses are scheduled Monday through Thursday between 8:30 a.m. and 2:15 p.m. The position is scheduled to begin in January 2027 for the Spring 2027 semester. Department of Biomedical and Health Sciences The Department of Biomedical and Health Sciences encompasses science and mathematics programs. The mathematics program offers a minor and supports general education and major-specific requirements. Faculty are expected to support student success through meaningful assessment, early intervention for at-risk students, and adherence to departmental policies. College Information CCSJ is a Catholic institution offering associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We foster a family-oriented environment and are committed to academic excellence and service. Faculty are expected to support the college’s mission: (https://www.ccsj.edu/about-ccsj/mission/) Requirements Application Requirements: Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three references. Final candidates will be asked to provide official transcripts. For more information contact, Dr. Carrie Hutton ( chutton@ccsj.edu ) or call 219-473-4284. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
